# Keep the Thunderbolt 3 bridge hierarchy and its USB controller out of D3hot.
#
# On 2026-11-18 0000:07:00.0 logged:
#
#   pcieport 0000:07:00.0: Unable to change power state from D3hot to D0,
#   device inaccessible
#
# The kernel then removed the whole Alpine Ridge hierarchy, including
# 0000:3c:00.0 (the JHL6540 USB controller) that the touch panel hangs off, and
# the panel re-enumerated as a new device ten seconds later.  Touch was dead for
# that window.
#
# The failure is a resume *from* D3hot, so the fix is not to enter it.  Runtime
# PM stays off for these devices; the idle power cost is negligible on a kiosk
# that is never suspended.
#
# Matched on vendor/device rather than bus address so it survives a
# re-enumeration renumbering the bridge chain.
#
# Reversible: delete this file (or set power/control back to "auto") and reload
# the rules.  If a D3hot failure still happens with this in place, the cause is
# power delivery or controller firmware, and the panel's USB should be moved off
# the Thunderbolt controller entirely.

ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="pci", ATTR{vendor}=="0x8086", ATTR{device}=="0x15d3", ATTR{power/control}="on"
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="pci", ATTR{vendor}=="0x8086", ATTR{device}=="0x15d4", ATTR{power/control}="on"
